{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795047082,"nonce":"QCEq0n/IfaBfP1Syd9qVcFtXhQI=","message":"Implementation candidate and scoped validation, 2026-11-19. Source remains uncommitted on e428e226; no source push or GitHub message.\n\nElements now register their own semantics through Div::accessibility(...) or ElementBuilder::accessibility_semantics(). AccessibilitySemantics carries role, child traversal, advertised actions, live-region defaults and an optional value/action provider. Standard roles describe shared semantics, not CN component types. Custom roles accept a component-owned name and use a named native group fallback without a new core lookup entry. Registration uses optional Arc descriptors and a sparse per-node map, with no global mutable registry. Boxed elements, metadata-only updates, provider replacement and subtree cleanup are covered.\n\nThe shared snapshot preserves parent IDs, container descendants, distinct checkbox/radio menu items, checked/selected/expanded/disabled state, live metadata and noneditable focus. Assistive actions use existing widget handlers and the focus router. Visible overflow children are no longer lost because an intermediate wrapper has no size; viewport bounds also preserve overlays below an auto-sized root.\n\nCN dialog, alert-dialog, popover, tooltip and toast builders supply their own descriptions. Dialog titles and descriptions provide reactive names and hints. Toasts use polite Status or assertive Alert, with assistive dismissal. Atomic toast updates are coalesced at the owning message; busy regions suppress announcements until ready. Unchanged native nodes are not resent.\n\nDesktop windows install AccessKit before becoming visible. Native callbacks queue work for the UI thread and wake redraw. Collection starts only after a native accessibility client activates the bridge. Stable Blinc IDs reach native nodes; focus updates, changed nodes, reactivation and removal are covered, and deactivation releases the cache. Covered-window accessibility work skips GPU rendering. A desktop-only module gate prevents AccessKit from entering iOS-only builds.\n\nValidation is scoped to the changed code and its existing focus regression targets. Mac: 76 unique tests passed (39 layout, 13 bridge/platform, 24 actual Metal headless), plus the hidden AppKit probe. The native probe checks hierarchy, custom roles/actions, focus, value editing, numeric slider values and stable object identity. The 12 App conversion cases also passed after the final feature gate. Captures for dialog, alert dialog, tooltip, popover and initial/updated toast were inspected. BLINC_SNAPSHOT=off disabled golden comparison; semantic, action and native assertions stayed active.\n\nNUC/Linux: 40 affected tests and App library compilation passed, using the existing source, target cache and SDK. All 28 transferred source-file hashes matched. Mac and NUC Cargo runs were serialized with two build jobs. Windows desktop-platform library, iOS Simulator App and WebAssembly layout compilation passed. Scoped Clippy has no diagnostics on changed lines; baseline warnings elsewhere remain. All 27 touched Rust files pass formatting and whitespace checks. The first four regression cases failed before implementation; the semantic-only/provider replacement case also exposed a missing hash before that was corrected.\n\nEvidence: .blinc/qa/accessibility-79-2026-11-18/{validation,source-sha256,final-test-gates,cross-check,lint,format}.json, native-final.log, captures/ and nuc-result/. No new worktree or Markdown plan.\n\nLimits: there was no live VoiceOver, NVDA or Orca run. Hidden AppKit API checks do not establish spoken behavior on every platform. Generic/custom atomic-region metadata is forwarded; the explicit whole-message coalescing coverage is for toasts. This does not add browser or Android accessibility adapters, nor claim a Calendar CPU or pause fix. Keep this track OPEN pending a source checkpoint and any further platform-reader validation.","files":null}]}